WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.470
So we were seeing more and more of this pejorative
use of the term Chinese virus from Donald

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:09.710
Trump to refer to the Corona virus, that's
bad enough and it's growing daily.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:14.719
Donald Trump seems to sort of be getting energy
from it and really enjoying using it.

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:20.950
But we're also now hearing from an Asian reporter
that a Trump official referred to the virus

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.400
as the Kang flu to her face.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.000
We're talking about Wagih Yang Jang, who is
a CBS News White House correspondent.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.260
She tweeted yesterday that quote, This morning,
a White House official referred to Corona

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.350
virus as the Kang flu to my face.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.370
Makes me wonder what they're calling it behind
my back.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:46.100
Meanwhile, again, Donald Trump seems to have
realized that Chinese virus is working well

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.190
for him in terms of propaganda and currying
favor with his supporters.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.909
And he's constantly tweeting about it.

00:00:51.909 --> 00:00:57.129
Now, just in the last few hours, Donald Trump
tweeted, quote, I always treated the Chinese

00:00:57.129 --> 00:01:01.890
virus very seriously and have done a very
good job from the beginning, including my

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:07.120
very early decision to close the borders from
China, as well as saying this morning, I will

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.280
be having a news conference today to discuss
very important news from the FDA concerning

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.320
the Chinese virus.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.550
And then an hour before that, for the people
that are now out of work because of the important

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.290
and necessary containment policies.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:23.710
For instance, the shutting down of hotels,
bars and restaurants.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:26.110
Money will soon be coming to you.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:30.880
The onslaught of the Chinese virus is not
your fault.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.500
Now, there are people saying we should call
it the Chinese virus because the Spanish flu

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.440
was called the Spanish flu.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.790
And we call things what they are.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:43.600
Even that assessment ignores history.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:49.010
The 1918 flu, sometimes called the Spanish
flu, didn't start in Spain and it didn't really

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.390
have anything to do with Spain.

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:54.490
The Spanish flu started in either Kansas,
France or China.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:02:00.410
It was called the Spanish Flu by the allies
in World War One because it got more attention

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:04.710
when it moved from France to Spain in November
of 1918.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:10.159
In the same way, if anything, we would be
calling this the European flu because it became

00:02:10.159 --> 00:02:15.760
more quickly prevalent around the world once
it got to Europe.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:18.040
And that really became the epicenter.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.400
It did originate in China.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:23.799
China had an explosion of cases now under
control in China.

00:02:23.799 --> 00:02:26.020
Europe is really the focus of the worldwide
spread.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:31.630
If things continue as European countries get
under control to explode in the U.S., this

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:35.709
may soon be the U.S. flu, the U.S. virus,
by the way.

00:02:35.709 --> 00:02:42.170
But in any case, you know, when you start
hearing things like Kong flu, Chinese virus,

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:46.340
you know, you're losing the fight against
the virus and you're instead choosing to fight

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.849
a propaganda war.

00:02:47.849 --> 00:02:54.150
And the reality is, wherever it started, like,
listen, if the governor of Oklahoma is bragging

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:59.170
about going out to restaurants when we should
be self isolating, it doesn't matter whether

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:03.819
it's started in China, France, Italy, Australia
or Peru.

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:04.819
It just doesn't matter.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:09.310
We are spreading it here and we are causing
the problem to get even worse.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:11.080
And that's ultimately what matters.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:12.790
And at the rate things are going.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:19.200
And from the EMA, I'm actually I actually
got a message yesterday from someone who said

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.269
someone I know's roommate is just pretending
like nothing's going on.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.590
They're just going about their day.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:29.120
They're annoyed that their favorite restaurants
are takeout only and they think the entire

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:30.779
thing is just a hoax.

00:03:30.779 --> 00:03:32.390
That's here in Massachusetts.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:37.300
Just imagine what is going on and how prevalent
that is in a red state like Oklahoma, where

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.190
the governor is publicly minimizing it and
bragging about being with his kids out to

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:43.749
dinner at a packed restaurant.

00:03:43.749 --> 00:03:45.889
We're just not going to solve it if that's
the case.

00:03:45.889 --> 00:03:48.310
And people will die unnecessarily.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:51.889
This is not, you know, lying about I cut the
deficit when you didn't.

00:03:51.889 --> 00:03:52.889
That's bad enough.

00:03:52.889 --> 00:03:55.299
But this this is life and death for a lot
of people.

00:03:55.299 --> 00:03:58.059
And every single day, the death toll is climbing.

00:03:58.059 --> 00:05:10.779
And it's not slowing down, unfortunately.

